  "reasoning": "The defendant sold a large quantity of shoes that were counterfeit versions of registered trademarks (GIVENCHY, LOUIS VUITTON, HERMES). Under Chinese criminal law, the act of knowingly selling counterfeit goods that infringe on a registered trademark constitutes the crime of ‘侵犯注册商标专用权罪’ (infringement of the exclusive right of a registered trademark). No other criminal conduct is described, so only this charge applies.",
